The dedication covers this compilation: the arrangement, the schemas, the
manifests, the tolerance bands and the prose. The recorded values
themselves are measurements and dates — facts about where a body was and
when a moment fell — which no one owns.

Where each corpus came from is recorded in corpus.json and in each file's
own `provenance`:

- baseline/  Recorded from an established open-source astrology engine
             (version 1.8.0) computing over Swiss Ephemeris 2.10.03 with
             its public data files. The engine and the ephemeris library
             are under their own terms and no part of either is
             reproduced here: what is here is the numbers they produced
             for the inputs stated beside them.

- official/  Read from the Rashtriya Panchangam for BS 2082 and 2083
             published by Nepal's national panchanga committee at
             npns.gov.np. The file records the document URLs, the page
             numbers and the date they were read. The published pages
             carry no text layer, so each line was read at two
             magnifications; the values are the committee's, transcribed.

- teimeris/  Recorded from Teimeris 0.1.0, an implementation of the
             Swiss Ephemeris algorithms, in its corrected profile.

- jpl/       Values computed by CSPICE over DE440 and DE441
             (NASA/JPL-Caltech); no endorsement implied. They were computed
             with spiceypy (Annex et al. 2020, Journal of Open Source
             Software 5(46), 2050, doi 10.21105/joss.02050), which bundles
             NAIF's CSPICE Toolkit, over NAIF's kernels. DE440 and DE441 are
             Park et al. 2021, The Astronomical Journal 161:105, doi
             10.3847/1538-3881/abd414. NAIF's rules
             (https://naif.jpl.nasa.gov/naif/rules.html) let anyone use its
             kernels and redistribute them unmodified. This corpus
             redistributes no kernel and no SPICE code, only the states
             computed from them; the manifest names each kernel by URL and
             SHA-256.
